# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the Clang TSan CI job.
#
# Pattern syntax: `<type>:<symbol-or-path>`. See:
# https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/ThreadSanitizerSuppressions
#
# Common types we use:
#   race:        suppress data-race reports rooted at <symbol>
#   thread:      suppress thread-leak reports
#   mutex:       suppress mutex misuse reports
#   deadlock:    suppress lock-order reports
#
# Keep this file empty by default; add an entry only when an upstream
# library produces a documented false positive that we cannot fix.
# Every entry should carry a one-line comment with a link or rationale
# so the next reader can audit and prune it.

# A queued lambda from QtStreamingLogSink is handed to the main thread through
# Qt's event queue. Qt is not instrumented, so TSan cannot see that its private
# mutex orders the allocation before the dispatch. CMakePresets.json documents
# this false positive for the Qt suites excluded from clang-tsan.
race:QtPrivate::QCallableObject<QtStreamingLogSink::*

# A finished QFuture's internal QWaitCondition is destroyed on the GUI thread after the pool thread woke it. Qt orders
# the two through its own futex-based mutex and reference count, which TSan cannot see because Qt is not instrumented.
# Our code never uses QWaitCondition directly, so this only hides reports inside Qt. See issue #114.
race:QWaitCondition::~QWaitCondition
